### 🚀 Getting the System Online (Zero to Chat)

Once your folders are set up, here is the exact sequence to bring the PlantbreedAIAgent online on a fresh machine:

**1. Install Global Dependencies:**
Make sure Python (3.9+) and R (4.0+) are installed. Ensure [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) is installed, running in the background, and has a model pulled (e.g., open a terminal and run `ollama pull llama3`).

**2. Install Project Requirements:**
From the root `PlantbreedAIAgent/` folder:

```bash
pip install fastapi uvicorn streamlit langchain langchain-ollama rpy2 pandas

```

*(Note: You will also need to ensure your R environment has packages like `lme4`, `metan`, `ggplot2` installed).*

**3. Start the Backend API (Terminal 1):**
This boots up the AI brain and connects it to the tools.

```bash
uvicorn api.server:app --reload

```

**4. Start the Frontend UI (Terminal 2):**
This launches the web interface in your browser.

```bash
streamlit run frontend/app.py

```

Upload a CSV to `workspace/inputs/`, type *"Analyze this trial,"* and watch the engine go to work!